  "english": "GG\nTHE SEVEN-YEAR CYCLE OF THE ROMANS 2.\n\nApril\n\n7. Sunday. Tone 4 [Dk / DZ]. Third [Sunday]. Green Sunday [Ashkharhamatran]. - Feast of the Annunciation of the Holy Virgin Mary.\n\nMay\n\n2. Thursday. Tone 8 [Dk / GK]. Day of the Ascension of Christ our God into heaven.\n\n12. Sunday. Tone 2 [Ak / AK]. Feast of the Coming of the Holy Spirit [Pentecost]. Barekendan [Eve] of the Fast of Elijah.\n\n19. Sunday. Tone 3 [Ag / AJ]. First. Beginning of the Sundays of the Resurrection. Canticle [Harts] Tone 1 [ahd / AD]: \"Who came for salvation\" (Or ekir i prkutiun). See according to the order in the First Volume.\n\nJune\n\n30. Sunday. Tone 6 [Bg / BZ]. Vardavar [Transfiguration]. The eating period is six weeks. See everything in the First Directory up to the Barekendan [Eve] of the Feast of the Assumption of the Mother of God, only keeping the dates two numbers higher.\n\nAugust\n\n11. Sunday. Tone 5 [Gd / DZ]. Seventh [Sunday]. Barekendan [Eve] of the Fast of the Holy Mother of God. Canticle [Harts] Tone 8 [gk / GK]: \"Ineffable nature\" (Anchareli bnutyun). Evening Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 5 [gd / G3]: \"The Myrrh-bearing women\" (Yughaber), and \"Today the resurrection\" (Aysor yarutiun).\n\n12. Monday. Tone 6 [Gk / GK]. Fast of the Holy Mother of God. Canticle [Harts] Tone 4 [bd / B3]: \"Just are your ways\" (Ughigh en chanaparhk ko).\n\n18. Sunday. Tone 4 [Bk / BK]. Assumption of the Holy Mother of God. The eating period is three weeks. See the First Volume, keeping the order of this place.\n\nJanuary\n\n6. SUNDAY. Tone 2 [Ak / AK]. Feast of the Nativity and Theophany of Christ. The eating period is eight days.\n\n13. Sunday. Tone 3 [Ag / AZ]. Barekendan [Eve] of the Fast of the Catechumens. Eighth Day of the Nativity and Circumcision of Christ.\n\n14. Monday. Tone 2 [Ak / AK]. Fast of the Catechumens. Canticle [Harts] Tone 2 [ak / AK]: \"Glorified forever\" (Paravoryal yavitian).\n\n19. Saturday. Tone 7 [Dd / DZZ]. Holy John the Forerunner [the Baptist].\n\n20. Sunday. Tone 8 [Dk / DK]. Canticle [Harts] Tone 7 [dd / DZ]: \"Glorifying\" (Paravorelov). Evening Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 8 [dk / DK]: \"Glory of the Resurrection\" (Park yarutian).\n\n21. Monday. Tone 3 [Ag / AZ]. [Feast of] Saint Sargis, his son Mardiros, and the fourteen soldiers, - and of the Atomian Generals.\n\n22. Tuesday. Tone 2 [Ak / AK]. The Sukiasank. Canticle [Harts] Tone 8 [dk / DK]: \"To You, O God\" (Ar kez astuadz).\n\n27. Sunday. Tone 7 [Dd / DZ]. Mid-Lent [Michink]. Evening Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 7 [dd / D3]: \"The resurrection of the Son of God\" (Zyarutiun astuadzorduyn). See everything else in the First Volume up to Vardavar, keeping the order of this place.\n\nFebruary\n\n3. Sunday. Tone 8 [Dk / DK]. Sunday of Great Barekendan [Eve of Great Lent].\n\n14. Thursday. Tone 3 [Bd / BZ]. Fast. Presentation of the Lord [Tiarn'ndaraj]. See according to the order in the First Volume.\n\nMarch\n\n24. Sunday. Tone 3 [Ag / AZ]. Easter. Day of the Resurrection of Christ our God. See according to the order in the First Volume.",
